secret, I

00:41:20.600 --> 00:41:23.120
consider it probably the
most critical piece of intellectual

00:41:23.120 --> 00:41:26.360
property we have at INPO
because if anyone finds out

00:41:26.360 --> 00:41:28.467
what goes into that model, then

00:41:29.750 --> 00:41:31.430
there's no way to
build a better model.

00:41:32.670 --> 00:41:33.170
So

00:41:34.370 --> 00:41:37.280
delivering those results meant that
we can't tell people what

00:41:38.120 --> 00:41:39.450
goes into the model,

00:41:39.450 --> 00:41:43.010
which means that when
a station's value changes,

00:41:43.010 --> 00:41:44.790
they of course,
want to know why.

00:41:44.790 --> 00:41:47.000
That's just a
natural thing to ask.

00:41:47.900 --> 00:41:48.710
And we

00:41:49.310 --> 00:41:53.600
didn't really give people a great
way to explain that at a

00:41:53.600 --> 00:41:55.010
kind of a general level. So

00:41:56.150 --> 00:41:56.810
last year,

00:41:56.810 --> 00:42:00.680
we built a tool to help
them kind of interpret that score

00:42:00.680 --> 00:42:02.840
and the changes to that score.

00:42:02.840 --> 00:42:06.740
And every time we would build
this model, we'd get this

00:42:07.460 --> 00:42:09.710
mountain of emails asking
why this and that changed.

00:42:09.710 --> 00:42:12.680
And then we built this tool
that helps give context to the

00:42:12.680 --> 00:42:14.310
changes. And, you know,

00:42:14.310 --> 00:42:16.320
now it's kind of crickets
every time we publish the model

00:42:16.320 --> 00:42:19.410
results, which is good
news for everyone.

00:42:20.190 --> 00:42:24.300
Past that, we're going to
be building more kind of tools,

00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:25.580
models, APIs.

00:42:26.670 --> 00:42:27.760
But we haven't done it yet.

00:42:27.760 --> 00:42:30.390
So I'm not really sure what
the challenges are, right?

00:42:30.390 --> 00:42:33.543
So if anyone has
any lessons learned,

00:42:34.330 --> 00:42:38.200
I'm so ready and willing to hear
what you all have learned as part pushing

00:42:39.000 --> 00:42:42.330
out Posit Team or any
other sort of data science platform.

00:42:42.330 --> 00:42:43.680
